@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Check session and restore a permitted route
actor "Account holder" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "ApplicationShell / Router" as shell
  participant "AuthenticationGuard /\nPermissionGuard" as guard
  participant "LoginPage" as login
  participant "Routed view /\nrecord resource" as records
  participant "ISessionService /\nSessionService /\nsessionInterceptor" as session
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "SessionsController /\nGetCurrentSessionQueryHandler" as sessionApi
  participant "Route's record controller /\nquery handler" as recordApi
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box

== 1. Direct protected URL with no session (L2-029.3, L2-003.3) ==
actor -> shell : Open a protected URL (reload, bookmark, or shared link)
shell -> guard : AuthenticationGuard.canActivate(path)
guard -> session : signedIn()
session --> guard : false: no token in memory, so no request is sent
guard -> guard : Accept internal application paths only; store RouteContext.requestedPath
guard -> guard : loginNotice = session-ended if Navigation Timing reports a reload, otherwise deep-link
guard -> login : Redirect to /login with replaceUrl
login --> actor : "Sign in to continue" or "Your session ended"; the record is not named and no protected data is requested

== 2. Sign in, refresh capabilities, restore only a permitted path (L2-029.3, L2-002) ==
actor -> login : Submit email and password
login -> session : login(LoginCommand) (sign-in-and-end-session slice)
session --> login : 200: token held in memory; end(Expired) scheduled at expiresAtUtc
login -> login : Clear loginNotice
login -> session : await refreshCapabilities(); concurrent callers share one request
session -> access : GET /api/session with bearer token; generation N captured
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Active account
access -> sessionApi : Authenticated request; MediatR 12.5.0
sessionApi -> db : Read safe account summary
db --> sessionApi : Account ID, display name, email, role
sessionApi --> session : 200 CurrentSession: email, role and capability summary; no contact data
session --> login : currentSession set (generation still N)
login -> guard : PermissionGuard.permits(requestedPath, currentSession()); clear requestedPath
alt Role lacks the path's capability (accounts.manage or audit.read for a Collaborator), or the refresh failed and no summary is held
  login -> shell : Navigate to /home instead of the requested path, with replaceUrl
  shell --> actor : Home opens with its heading focused; no access-denied page follows sign-in (L2-029.3)
else Path permitted
  login -> shell : Navigate to the requested path, with replaceUrl, so Back never reaches the sign-in form of this live session
  shell -> guard : AuthenticationGuard passes; PermissionGuard.canActivate allows from the current summary
  guard --> shell : Allow
  ref over shell, db : 4. Route's existing record query
end

== 3. In-session navigation to a route the role cannot use (L2-029.4) ==
actor -> shell : Follow an in-app link or browser history to /accounts or /audit, or keep using a route after a role change
shell -> guard : PermissionGuard.canActivate(path)
guard -> session : refreshCapabilities()
session --> guard : Current summary lacks accounts.manage or audit.read
guard -> shell : Set RouteContext.status = AccessDenied for the attempted URL; return false, so no record is requested
shell --> actor : ShellStatusView access-denied page in place of the routed content, offering Home and Projects; focus heading (L2-029.4)

== 4. Route's existing record query (L2-029.2, L2-029.4) ==
shell -> records : Create the routed view; its record resource reads through its own service contract
records -> session : Request passes through sessionInterceptor; bearer token; generation N captured
session -> access : GET the record endpoint, e.g. /api/workspaces/{id}/work-items/{itemId}
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt 401: token expired, account deactivated, or credential version changed
  access --> session : 401 ProblemDetails; denial audited without payloads
  session -> session : Generation still N: end(Unauthorized), once; later 401s of generation N are discarded
  session --> records : 401: the read rejects with its 401; the resource keeps its state
  session --> shell : endReason = Unauthorized
  shell --> actor : Store requestedPath; navigate to /login with replaceUrl, destroying the page; sign-in shows "Your session ended"
else 403: capability routes only (/accounts, /audit), role changed after the check (L2-002.4)
  access --> session : 403 ProblemDetails; denial audited without payloads
  session -> session : refreshCapabilities() (deduplicated)
  session --> records : 403 passes on
  records --> shell : AccountView, AccountDetailView or AuditEventView emits forbidden; its page calls inject(ApplicationShell).showStatus(AccessDenied)
  shell --> actor : ShellStatusView access-denied page in place of the routed content, offering permitted destinations; navigation follows the refreshed role; focus heading
else Authorized
  access -> recordApi : Authenticated request
  recordApi -> db : Read record with its workspace and ancestor path
  alt 404: record missing or deleted
    db --> recordApi : No row
    recordApi --> session : 404 ProblemDetails (a malformed ID never gets this far: the {id:guid} route constraint answers 404 at once)
    session --> records : Generation still N: pass on
    records --> actor : The routed view renders its own not-found state inside the shell (e.g. Lead not found with Back to leads); focus heading
  else 200: record found
    db --> recordApi : Record, workspace, ancestors
    recordApi --> session : 200 record projection
    alt Session ended while in flight (generation no longer N)
      session --> records : Discard: the record resource keeps its state
    else Generation still N
      session --> records : Record projection
      records --> shell : Record and path
      shell -> shell : RouteContext = workspaceId and ancestorIds
      shell --> actor : Render page with ancestor links; focus heading (L2-033.4)
    end
  end
end

== 5. Address that matches no client route (L2-029.4) ==
actor -> shell : Open a mistyped address, e.g. /projcts
shell -> guard : AuthenticationGuard.canActivate(path)
guard --> shell : Token in memory: pass
shell -> shell : No client route matches, so the shell's last child route ** renders ShellStatusView NotFound with Home, Projects and Leads
shell --> actor : "That page doesn't exist"; no request sent; focus heading
note over shell, db
GET /api/session reads only the token subject, so it has no 400 path. If the post-login refresh fails, no summary
is held: LoginPage opens /home, which needs no capability, and its sections report their own read failures.
Later, a refresh that fails with no summary held shows ShellStatusView Error (reference ID) or Offline for a
capability route; other routes open. Lead, workspace, work, and sprint reads need only an active session, so they
have no 403 branch. A record read answered 500 renders the routed view's own error state with its reference ID and
Try again (L2-043); a read with no response renders it with Try again and no reference ID. A malformed record ID inside a matched client route reaches the routed view, whose read gets 404.
Status pages stay until the next navigation starts; Try again navigates to the attempted URL with onSameUrlNavigation 'reload',
so route matching and guards run again even at the same URL. A BoardModeGuard (canMatch) that declines on a 500, 503 or no
response leaves the router at the board URL on the ** route with the Error or Offline status it set. All keep the navigation.
/login opened while a session is held redirects to /home, except the sign-out navigation, which carries { signOut: true }.
end note
@enduml
